</mixed-citation></citation-alternatives></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation-alternatives><element-citation id="ec-CR9" publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ritchey</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Maresh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeely</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Shaffer</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Keteyian</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Tracking cardiac rehabilitation participation and completion among medicare beneficiaries to inform the efforts of a national initiative</article-title><source>Circ Cardiovasc Qual Outcomes</source><year>2020</year><volume>13</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>e005902</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/CIRCOUTCOMES.119.005902</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">31931615</pub-id>
</element-citation><mixed-citation id="mc-CR9" publication-type="journal">Ritchey MD, Maresh S, McNeely J, Shaffer T, Jackson SL, Keteyian SJ, et al. Tracking cardiac rehabilitation participation and completion among medicare beneficiaries to inform the efforts of a national initiative. Circ Cardiovasc Qual Outcomes. 2020;13(1):e005902. 10.1161/CIRCOUTCOMES.119.005902.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">31931615</pub-id>
